## Atomic nodes

## 1. Blend (atomic)

- Date: 11 October 2026
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/atomic-nodes/blend/blend
- Category: Atomic nodes
- Purpose: Combines a Foreground and a Background with a chosen blending mode, optionally limited by a mask.
- Inputs: Foreground (Grayscale or Color), Background (Grayscale or Color, primary), Opacity (Grayscale, optional alpha mask). Foreground and Background must have the same type.
- Parameters: Opacity (Float, multiplies the Opacity input), Blending mode (Integer, static), Alpha blending (Integer, static: Use source alpha, Ignore alpha, Straight alpha blending, Premultiplied alpha blending), Cropping area (Float4, static, acts as an extra opacity mask).
- Blend modes (values of the Blending mode parameter, source https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/atomic-nodes/blend/blending-modes-description, read 11 October 2026): Copy, Add (Linear dodge), Subtract, Multiply, Add sub, Max (Lighten), Min (Darken), Switch, Divide, Overlay, Screen, Soft light. The page lists 12 modes.
- Defaults and ranges: not stated.
- Copernicus nearest: Cop blend (fit: close)
- Mapping status: documented_only

## 2. Blur (atomic)

- Date: 11 October 2026
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/atomic-nodes/blur
- Category: Atomic nodes, simplest and fastest blur
- Purpose: Applies a box blur that averages neighbouring pixel values over a set distance, giving a fuzzy result.
- Inputs: not stated on the fetched page.
- Parameters: Intensity (blur distance, range 0 to unlimited; type and default not stated). Values above the useful range turn the image into one averaged colour.
- Notes: The page points to Blur HQ (section 11) for demanding work.
- Copernicus nearest: Cop blur (fit: close)
- Mapping status: documented_only

